# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Junjie Wang et al. (2024). E(n)-Equivariant cartesian tensor message passing interatomic potential.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-024-51886-6  arXiv:2402.15286v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2402.15286v1 (sha256 bd13be4e8b9d717d...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 119 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the HotPP method (introduced here) and its two
# potential-energy benchmarks: a model trained on 70% of ANI-1x and
# tested on the six COMP6 subsets (Table I), and a model for carbon
# across phases (Table II). The dipole and polarizability predictions
# (Table III) are outside the protocol.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

