###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I prints COMP6 energy MAEs in meV with values between 209 and 1155 for HotPP (e.g. ANI-MD 1155) against the kcal/mol-scale values usually quoted; they are encoded as printed and the unit should be checked against the version of record.
# - Other columns of Tables I and II (ANI-1x; GAP, DP, MTP, REANN, NEP, NequIP l = 1-3 on carbon) are literature values and are not encoded. The carbon virial RMSE (64 meV/atom) has no MetricProperty.
# - The cutoff radius, loss and optimiser are in a figure or the methods that were not captured ('almost the same hyperparameters' for all data sets); 8 Bessel roots are encoded as numRadialBasis and the 3-layer radial MLP with 64 nodes is left out.
# - A second carbon model retrained on a more accurate data set (for the diamond phonons), the separate liquid-water potential used for IR and Raman spectra, and the dipole and polarizability models (Table III) are not encoded. Phonons from automatic-differentiation force constants (phonopy) and classical MD of water are the grounds for the simulation types.
# - Version read: arXiv v1, whose title differs from the version of record.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

